<p><b>SetBorthogonalization</b> selects the orthogonalization to use in the solver GD/JD of Slepc, whereas <b>GetBorthogonalization</b> returns this orthogonalization. This method is used when Seldon calls the following Slepc functions : <a href="https://slepc.upv.es/documentation/current/docs/manualpages/EPS/EPSGDSetBOrth.html">EPSGDSetBOrth</a>, <a href="https://slepc.upv.es/documentation/current/docs/manualpages/EPS/EPSJDSetBOrth.html">EPSJDSetBOrth</a>. </p>

